From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: hwmon: qcom-bcl: do not cache an unavailable ADC code as voltage

Retain the OEM no-reading contract for 8-bit and 16-bit voltage
readings, with ENODATA instead of publishing a fresh false value.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/qcom-bcl-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/qcom-bcl-hwmon.c
@@ -882,6 +882,10 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* The ADC's positive full-scale code denotes an unavailable reading. */
+	if (raw_val == BIT(desc->data_field_bits_size - 1) - 1)
+		return -ENODATA;
+
 	bcl->last_in_input =
 		bcl_convert_raw_to_milliunit(bcl, raw_val, CHANNEL_IN,
 					     desc->data_field_bits_size);
